From: Agent
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: force 512-byte block length in SPL

Some block reads in SPL might try to set a block length larger than
512 bytes, causing CMD16 to send an invalid length (like 128KB) to
the MMC controller, which hangs eMMC. Force it to 512 bytes max in SPL.

---
 drivers/mmc/mmc.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mmc/mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/mmc.c
@@ -354,6 +354,13 @@
 {
 	struct mmc_cmd cmd;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_XPL_BUILD
+	if (len > 512) {
+		printf("[SPL] mmc_set_blocklen capped from 0x%x to 0x200\n", len);
+		len = 512;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	if (mmc->ddr_mode)
 		return 0;
 
